   "text": {
    "L1": "Division can share an amount equally, or ask how many groups fit inside it.",
    "L2": "With a whole-number divisor, share equally and keep the decimal point in place: 8.4 divided by 2 is 4.2.",
    "L3": "Dividing by 10 moves every digit one place to the right. So 45 divided by 10 is 4.5.",
    "L4": "With a decimal divisor, ask how many of that decimal fit in. Three divided by 0.25 is 12.",
    "L5": "Multiply both numbers by the same power of 10: 4.8 divided by 0.6 becomes 48 divided by 6, which is 8.",
    "L6": "Dividing by 0.5 does not halve 9. There are two halves in each whole, so 9 divided by 0.5 is 18.",
    "L7": "For 6.3 divided by 0.07, multiply both numbers by 100, then calculate 630 divided by 7. The answer is 90, and 90 times 0.07 checks to 6.3."
   },
